diff --git a/audit/reference-contract.md b/audit/reference-contract.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..84f262ad107a7d3cf7218af24ce9ab8fe396862f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/audit/reference-contract.md
@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@
+# Encoded IW7 GSC references — source contract, 2026-10-12
+
+This contract answers one precise question: does the complete input encode any
+external script reference or an unresolved/dynamic reference under the pinned
+IW7 PC server decoder profile? It is not a proof of all dependencies, native
+builtin behavior, asset availability, retail compatibility or runtime acceptance.
+
+The existing `--stdin-gscbin` and `iw7.gsc-consumption-native/1` remain unchanged.
+The separate `--stdin-gscbin-references` mode emits `iw7.gsc-reference-native/1`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": "iw7.gsc-reference-native/1",
+  "profile_sha256": "independently pinned profile file SHA256",
+  "consumption": {"schema": "iw7.gsc-consumption-native/1"},
+  "functions": [{
+    "bytecode_begin": 1,
+    "token_id": 0,
+    "name_hex": "6d61696e",
+    "instructions": [{
+      "bytecode_begin": 1,
+      "bytecode_bytes": 1,
+      "opcode": 25,
+      "stack_begin": 13,
+      "stack_end": 13
+    }]
+  }]
+}
+```
+
+The consumption object above is abbreviated for documentation only. The real
+stream requires the full existing closed schema. Symbols use hex, so arbitrary
+decoder bytes cannot break JSON or be silently replaced by Unicode conversion.
+Native reports have at most 10,000 functions and 100,000 instructions. They are
+emitted only after decoding and local resolution finish. There is no success
+stream on a decoder error.
+
+## Independent reader and pins
+
+`references.validate(raw, native, pins, source_root, consumption_validator)` is
+read-only and does not execute any process. `raw` must be the same original input
+bytes. `source_root` supplies the retained source tables, rehashed individually.
+The supplied module is the existing pure SDK consumption validator. Expected pins
+must come from the reviewed build/consumer configuration, never from the report:
+
+```text
+decoder = {tool_sha256, source_revision, source_sha256, tables_sha256}
+profile_sha256
+reference_validator_sha256
+consumption_validator_sha256
+```
+
+The reader verifies the module files, profile, every table file and table digest;
+then invokes the existing strict consumption validator. It independently parses
+the container, function headers, **every** opcode and every stack operand. Native
+function symbols, instruction extents, stack spans and function partitions must
+equal the independent parse exactly. Unknown fields and bool-for-integer witness
+substitution are refused. Branches must land on instruction boundaries in their
+own function; local script addresses must resolve to actual function entries.
+
+`load_report(path)` rejects duplicate JSON keys and bounds the file to 64 MiB.
+Callers using another JSON loader must enforce the same uniqueness rule.
+`inspect_bytes` is exposed for pure byte-level tests only. Its result is not a
+native-bound qualification and must not be promoted directly into a Creator gate.
+
+The bound result contains all typed `references`, `blockers` with bytecode and
+stack positions, category counts and `complete_instruction_coverage_verified`.
+`encoded_external_script_reference_absence` is true only when the full checks
+pass and the blocker list is empty. It is not a hardcoded false placeholder.
+Malformed input, unsupported decoding or a mismatched witness raises an error;
+it never returns a partially qualified result.
+
+## Opcode/operand taxonomy
+
+The frozen profile lists each of the 153 registered opcode IDs explicitly. There
+is no default category that treats a new opcode as safe.
+
+| Category | Encoded operands and qualification |
+| --- | --- |
+| Local script calls and `GetLocalFunction` | Signed 24-bit offset shifted by one (`offs9`), relative to the operand position; optional thread argument count. Must resolve to an input function. |
+| External script calls and `GetFarFunction` | Two stack `u32` tokens, each followed by a NUL string only for token zero; three code relocation bytes and optional argument count. Both calls and taking an address block absence. |
+| Native builtin calls/addresses | `u16` ID resolved against the function or method table; explicit or opcode-implied argument count. Known entries are listed separately; unknown entries block. |
+| Calls through pointers | Zero or one encoded argument-count byte. Target is dynamic and blocks, even if Far call count is zero or a preceding address looks local. No unproved dataflow inference. |
+| Animation and animtree operands | One or two stack strings and code placeholders. Listed as asset references; unresolved/encrypted names block. Known names do not grant asset closure. |
+| Strings and fields | Exact NUL stack strings; fields use code `u32` token or indirect stack value. Unknown token, encrypted placeholder or unresolved indirect field blocks. Plain strings are not guessed to be GSC imports based on path syntax. Empty ordinary strings are valid. |
+| Branches and switch tables | Signed/unsigned branch operands; switch rows consume seven code bytes each and conditionally consume a stack string. Every destination and cursor is checked. Unknown default sentinel blocks. |
+| Plain, scalar and local-slot operations | Explicit fixed widths with no encoded reference. Their bytes are still fully covered. |
+| Registered but unsupported sizes | `OP_ClearVariableField` (0x3C) and `OP_EvalNewLocalVariableRefCached0` (0x7C) already throw in the native size resolver. They remain explicit refusals. |
+
+Every instruction is inspected, including unreachable instructions. A Far=0
+counter cannot replace this process. Known `precachemodel`, `loadfx`, `spawn` and
+other native calls may depend on assets or engine behavior; the name table does
+not establish those semantics. This reader performs no argument dataflow analysis.
+
+## Table provenance
+
+The source authority is the community xensik/gsc-tool baseline
+`3300e430d1efef00e54c66a8bd416e18a2a9882a`, not an official retail engine schema.
+`reference-profile.json` records exact upstream blobs and last-changing commits
+for the IW7 tables/context declaration, plus actual SHA256s for all eight files
+covered by the native table digest. Builtin comments containing engine addresses
+or `nullptr` are provenance data, not evidence those functions work in this server.
+
+The compiled tables have 806 function names, 1,483 method names and 13,220 token
+entries. The source token file also contains commented-out empty slots; the
+reader excludes them. It never fills gaps or treats those comments as resolved
+symbols. Literal/token fallback values with unresolved placeholder prefixes,
+invalid UTF-8 names and encrypted strings remain explicit blockers.
+
+`make_reference_profile.py` reproduces the reviewed profile from retained local
+Git objects without fetching. It refuses a missing category or a table changed
+from the pinned upstream baseline. Regeneration is an explicit source change;
+`prepare.py` refuses a stale table digest before creating build identity. The
+profile's bytes and Python reader enter the tool source digest, and the profile
+SHA is also compiled into the reference witness.
+
+## Evidence and the route to qualification
+
+Source-only tests have read the exact retained Beacon binaries without executing
+them or a native tool. The variant has 570 instructions (8 local script calls,
+54 known builtin calls), zero external/pointer references and zero unresolved
+symbols. The original has 560 instructions and two external references to
+`scripts/engine/utility`: `flag_exist` at bytecode 212 / stack 318, and `flag` at
+bytecode 226 / stack 345. The recorded input hashes remain the v6 input hashes.
+These are independently decoded byte observations, not a new native witness.
+
+`test_references.py` exercises the full 153-opcode profile, numeric namespaces,
+address-only imports, pointer targets, unknown symbols, assets, switch operands,
+truncation, false spans, hidden instructions, witness changes and pin mismatches.
+It uses a real pure consumption validator and explicitly synthetic native-shaped
+fixtures for tampering controls. `test_plan.py` checks profile/header binding and
+rejects stale profiles.
+
+`test_reference_native.py` is prepared but has **not** executed. It compares the
+new native stream with the independent reader for all opcode specimens and both
+real Beacon inputs, and retains separate native/bound JSON artifacts. Before any
+execution, a new reviewed Plan must pin this source, both readers, the profile,
+input bytes and executable; include the additional test/witness phase and its
+artifacts in supervision; obtain resource admission and explicit GO. The existing
+seven-phase v6 recipe does not execute or qualify the new reference contract.
+No v6 witness is retroactively upgraded.
+
+Once this exact native-to-reader agreement is proven and its successful build
+record linked, Creator may clear the **encoded GSC reference** gate for the
+variant. External-reference originals and dynamic/unknown inputs stay blocked
+with concrete reasons. Any broader GSC dependency claim still requires proof of
+native script-loading/callback semantics. Asset closure requires the relevant
+model/animation/material and retail evidence; package finalization requires its
+own reviewed consumer rules. This change does not modify Creator.
+
+The result therefore keeps `native_execution_authenticated`,
+`native_builtin_semantics_verified`, `asset_dependency_closure_verified`,
+`retail_runtime_compatibility_verified`, `runtime_validation_passed`,
+`owner_acceptance` and `package_ready` false. They are separate evidentiary gates;
+the encoded-reference result itself can become true when its stated proof succeeds.
